    "description": "Estimating's stage of the flow: Scope & takeoff → Underwriting sheet → Quote built → Handed to the Closer. Labor is guys × days rather than a typed figure, so changing the crew or the days moves every number below it. Line items are a sub-item list with the vendor on the line it prices. The takeoff is a spreadsheet laid out as the eight GAF measurements with a live waste column. Margin tier names the policy and Target margin % is the number the arithmetic reads — a category cannot drive a formula. Two limits are shown rather than papered over: the line items total is typed, because a calculation resolves {Label} against the app's fields and there is no per-record rollup over a sub-item list; and the hand-off button installs without a destination, because a bundle cannot name an app id in a workspace it has never seen — pick the Sales Pipeline once after installing.",
